%description:

One indoor distance per radio, shared by its carriers, through the real PHY.

The channel model's indoor tests give it stub endpoints. Here real NrUe and
gNodeB nodes run on two carriers below 6 GHz, 2 GHz and 3.5 GHz, indoors and
outdoors, in TR 38.901 UMa with a fixed LOS state, with fading, shadowing and
interference off. There TR 38.901 Table 7.4.3-3 applies:

    PLtw = "20 dB"
    PLin = "0.5 d2D-in"
    sigma_P = "0 dB"

so the deviate does not enter, and the indoor loss is a sum of 20 dB and the
distance's term alone. Everything else cancels between an outdoor and an indoor
run of the same geometry, whatever the carrier and whichever way the link goes,
so each UE's distance can be read from its results:

    d = (SINR_outdoor - SINR_indoor - 20) / 0.5

A UE's receiver records the SINRs of both directions of the UE's links, per
carrier, under the carrier's frequency. The grader computes d from each of them:
measuredSinrDl (the CQI, evaluated at the gNB, with the UE as the receiver),
measuredSinrUl (evaluated at the gNB, with the UE as the transmitter), rcvdSinrDl
(evaluated at the UE) and rcvdSinrUl (evaluated at the gNB). So this also covers
the rule that a link's penetration loss is its UE end's, for real nodes:
**.insideBuilding marks the gNB's radio as well, whose own distance is a decoy.

Per UE, all eight values must agree to 1e-9. They must lie in [0, 25), and differ
between the UEs: the distance is the UE's, not the scenario's. A value of 5 m or
more must occur among the UEs, which tells a distance from a draw of another
kind that a standard-normal deviate would be: it may lie in the range and differ
between UEs too, but it does not reach 5 m. With a distance uniform in [0, 25),
four UEs all stay below 5 m with probability 0.2^4 = 0.0016, once per draw order.

That the statistics really are the carriers' own is checked on the way: outdoors,
below the breakpoint distance, the two carriers differ by 20 log10(3.5 / 2) dB in
every statistic (TR 38.901 Table 7.4.1-1, PL1 of UMa).

What a specification says here, and what it does not. For the O2I penetration
models of Table 7.4.3-2, TR 38.901 7.4.3.1 says "d2D-in shall be
UT-specifically generated". Table 7.4.3-3 is offered "for UMa and UMi
single-frequency simulations at frequencies below 6 GHz", with "d2D-in being a
single, link-specific, uniformly distributed variable between 0 and 25 m". So the
scenario here, two carriers, is outside the table's title, and sharing the
distance between carriers follows the UT-specific statement, not the table's
link-specific one. That the model applies this table on each carrier below 6 GHz
is the model's choice; this is a regression test of that choice, as far as the
20 dB is concerned, and the one place that shows the distance is one per radio.

The fixed LOS state and the UEs' height of 1.5 m leave no draw in the path loss:
h_E is 1 m (TR 38.901 Table 7.4.1-1, note 1: C = 0 below 13 m), and the UEs stand
below the breakpoint distance on both carriers.

%extraargs: -c IndoorOneRadioTwoCarriers

%file: demo.xml
<config>
    <interface among='eNB* eNodeB* enb* *Enb* gNB* gNodeB* gnb* *Gnb* upf* *Upf* mecHost* pgw*' address='10.x.x.x' netmask='255.255.255.0'/>
    <interface hosts='*' address='192.168.x.x' netmask='255.255.255.0'/>
</config>

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[Config IndoorOneRadioTwoCarriers]
network = simu5g.simulations.nr.networks.SingleCell_Standalone
sim-time-limit = 1s
**.routingRecorder.enabled = false
cmdenv-express-mode = true
cmdenv-status-frequency = 10000000s
seed-set = 0

output-scalar-file = results/${iterationvarsf}${repetition}.sca
output-vector-file = results/${iterationvarsf}${repetition}.vec
**.vector-recording = false

############### The sweep ##############
**.insideBuilding = ${indoor = false, true}

############### Two carriers below 6 GHz, both on every node ##############
*.carrierAggregation.numComponentCarriers = 2
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].carrierFrequency = 2GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].numBands = 6
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[1].carrierFrequency = 3.5GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[1].numBands = 6
*.gnb.cellularNic.numCarriers = 2
*.gnb.cellularNic.phy.componentCarrierModules = "carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0] carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[1]"
*.ue[*].cellularNic.nrPhy.componentCarrierModules = "carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0] carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[1]"

############### Geometry: every UE below the breakpoint distance on both carriers ##############
*.gnb.mobility.initialX = 300m
*.gnb.mobility.initialY = 300m
*.gnb.mobility.initialZ = 25m
*.numUe = 4
*.ue[*].servingNodeId = 0
*.ue[*].nrServingNodeId = 1
*.ue[0].mobility.initialX = 360m
*.ue[0].mobility.initialY = 300m
*.ue[1].mobility.initialX = 300m
*.ue[1].mobility.initialY = 400m
*.ue[2].mobility.initialX = 150m
*.ue[2].mobility.initialY = 300m
*.ue[3].mobility.initialX = 300m
*.ue[3].mobility.initialY = 80m
*.ue[*].mobility.initialZ = 1.5m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinX = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinY = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinZ = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxX = 1000m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxY = 1000m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxZ = 50m
**.mobility.initFromDisplayString = false

############### The channel: one path loss and the indoor loss ##############
**.scenario = "URBAN_MACROCELL"
**.nodebHeight = 25m
**.ueHeight = 1.5m
**.dynamicLos = false
**.fixedLos = true
**.fading = false
**.shadowing = false
**.downlinkInterference = false
**.uplinkInterference = false
**.bgCellInterference = false
**.extCellInterference = false

############### Traffic in both directions, for the receptions ##############
# More than a carrier of 6 bands carries, so that every UE's frames go out on both
*.ue[*].numApps = 2
*.server.numApps = 8
*.ue[*].app[0].typename = "CbrReceiver"
*.ue[*].app[0].localPort = 3000
*.server.app[0..3].typename = "CbrSender"
*.server.app[0..3].destAddress = "ue[" + string(ancestorIndex(0)) + "]"
*.server.app[0..3].destPort = 3000
*.server.app[0..3].localPort = 3088 + ancestorIndex(0)
*.server.app[0..3].packetSize = 1000B
*.server.app[0..3].samplingTime = 0.002s
*.server.app[0..3].startTime = 0.1s
*.ue[*].app[1].typename = "CbrSender"
*.ue[*].app[1].destAddress = "server"
*.ue[*].app[1].destPort = 4000 + ancestorIndex(1)
*.ue[*].app[1].localPort = 4088
*.ue[*].app[1].packetSize = 1000B
*.ue[*].app[1].samplingTime = 0.002s
*.ue[*].app[1].startTime = 0.1s
*.server.app[4..7].typename = "CbrReceiver"
*.server.app[4..7].localPort = 4000 + ancestorIndex(0) - 4

*.configurator.config = xmldoc("./demo.xml")

%postrun-command: ../../physics_reference.py --grade results >verdict.txt

%contains: verdict.txt
graded=59 failures=0

%not-contains: verdict.txt
FAILED
